# {PROJECT_NAME}

SpecWeave project. Work happens in increments under `.specweave/increments/NNNN-slug/`. Spec + plan are the source of truth; the ledger records who did what. Keep this file under one page; project-specific notes go in **Project notes** at the bottom.
<!-- /SECTION -->

<!-- SECTION:structure -->
## Structure

```
.specweave/
  increments/NNNN-slug/   spec.md (WHAT + ACs) · plan.md (HOW, optional) · tasks.md (task list) · ledger.jsonl (claims/done) · handoff.md · reports/
  docs/                    ADRs and hand-written docs (read before changing architecture)
  config.json
```
Only those files live in an increment root; everything else goes in `reports/`. Commit messages start with the increment id: `0042: add login form`.
<!-- /SECTION -->

<!-- SECTION:loop required -->
## The loop

| Step | Command |
|---|---|
| Plan a feature (spec + plan, in plan mode) | `/sw:increment "title"` |
| Work the tasks (claim → implement → done with evidence) | `/sw:do` |
| Verify the whole increment | `specweave verify` |
| Review before closing (optional, recommended for user-facing work) | `/sw:review` |
| Close (needs a green verify or `--reason`) | `/sw:done` |
| Stop for any reason (context, tokens, switching tools) | `/sw:handoff` |

Start every feature with the increment, even a small one, unless the user says "no increment". Fix a bug by writing the failing test first, then fixing the code without touching the test.
<!-- /SECTION -->

<!-- SECTION:verify required -->
## Verification before "done"

Run the project's build/test/lint (see **Commands**) before reporting any task complete and paste the real output. `specweave task done T-NN --run "<test cmd>"` refuses a failing command. Never skip, weaken, or delete a test to make it pass. Never set `status: completed` by hand; use `/sw:done`.
<!-- /SECTION -->

<!-- SECTION:parallel required -->
## Working in parallel (any tool, any account)

1. One worktree per agent (`git worktree add ../NNNN-me -b inc/NNNN-me`).
2. Claim before editing: `specweave task claim T-NN` (or `specweave task next`). Edit only that task's **Files**.
3. Never edit ledger lines or another task's status; append only.
4. `done` needs the task's **Test** command exit 0 and a commit sha.
5. When you stop: `specweave task release --all-mine` then `/sw:handoff`. Read the latest `handoff.md` before resuming someone else's increment.
<!-- /SECTION -->

<!-- SECTION:conventions required -->
## Conventions

- Secrets: confirm a key is present without printing its value (`grep -q NAME .env` or `Select-String -Quiet NAME .env`); never commit `.env*`.
- Prefer deleting code over adapting it; change only what the task needs.
- Check `.specweave/docs/` ADRs before architectural changes; record new decisions in `plan.md` or an ADR.
- Nested repos live under `repositories/<org>/<repo>/`; commit inside each nested repo, then the umbrella.
<!-- /SECTION -->

<!-- SECTION:troubleshooting -->
## Troubleshooting

| Issue | Fix |
|---|---|
| Skills or hooks missing | `specweave doctor`, then restart Claude Code |
| Instructions out of date after upgrade | `specweave update` |
| Unsure who owns a task | `specweave task list` |
